# Reviewing changes in `trust/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`trust/REVIEW.md`** for any
changed path under `trust/`. That map cites rule IDs from `trust/AGENTS.md` (e.g.
`TRUST_PURITY.no_io`, `AP-1`, `G4`, `TAP-1`, `TAP-4`) — it never restates the rule text.

Deterministic checks that fire here first (precedence over LLM):
- D1 dependency table (`check_dependency_rules`) — trust has ZERO outward deps.
- D4 trust purity (`check_trust_purity`) — no I/O / logging / network in `trust/`.
- D3 TAP-2 mock abuse + TAP-4 failure-path ratio on `tests/trust/**`.

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
